      "short": "$A=\\$30.54$, $B=\\$5121.08$.",
      "worked": "The monthly rate is $0.6\\%=0.006$. Interest is calculated on the balance at the start of the month.\n\n$$\\begin{align*} A &= 5090.54\\times0.006 \\\\ A &= 30.54324 \\\\ A &\\approx \\$30.54 \\end{align*}$$\n\nAdd the interest to the starting balance, retaining the unrounded interest in the calculation.\n\n$$\\begin{align*} B &= 5090.54+30.54324 \\\\ B &= 5121.08324 \\\\ B &\\approx \\$5121.08 \\end{align*}$$",
